{"id":"chatcmpl-d280c83c-e284-4f8f-9459-4ea507da5bb8","object":"chat.completion","created":1795250895,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When a primary visual-question-answering tool returns a negative or ambiguous result despite visible evidence, escalate to a second, independent grounding/localization tool rather than accepting the first answer. Resolve laterality by anchoring findings to patient-side anatomy (e.g., axilla, lung field) and distinguishing midline structures from lateralized ones. Cross-check the final answer against the grounded localization before committing.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Escalation on negative/ambiguous results: if the first tool contradicts visible evidence or returns 'No', invoke an alternate grounding tool before answering.\",\n    \"Laterality disambiguation: separate midline structures (e.g., sternal wires) from truly lateralized findings (e.g., clips in one axilla) to determine left vs right.\",\n    \"Independent confirmation: use a second tool with a different mechanism (grounded report vs VQA) to corroborate the location before finalizing.\",\n    \"Anatomical anchoring: map detected objects to named patient-side landmarks rather than image coordinates to avoid left/right confusion.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Prefer grounded localization reports over single-shot VQA when laterality or presence is contested; anchor findings to patient-side anatomy.\",\n    \"Tool-orchestration tasks\": \"Treat a negative or low-confidence first-tool output as a trigger to call a complementary tool, not as a final answer.\",\n    \"Binary-choice localization\": \"Explicitly rule out the alternative option by checking for absence of the finding on the opposite side.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding's side using a grounded/localization source, and verify the opposite side lacks the finding.\",\n    \"Distinguish midline from lateralized structures before assigning left vs right.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":462,"total_tokens":833,"completion_tokens":371,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":462},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":371}}}